    "limitations": [
      "This is a previously exposed cohort regression, not new holdout evidence. Earlier outcomes informed follow-up policy changes.",
      "Two attempts per task are correlated repetitions; family and distinct-task outcomes are reported separately.",
      "Development selected standalone autonomous completion without LLM fallback; final results include the existing LLM continuation.",
      "Temperature and routing thresholds use reserved calibration examples/tasks, separate from development and final test. Reusing those values after a routing change does not establish calibration for the new routing policy.",
      "All arms use the same observed history, invoice authorization guard, initial state, and tool budget; later states depend on actual actions.",
      "Invoice-local mode adds a shared 16-model-call cap per task; legacy whole-task routing used recursion and tool bounds without this explicit shared cap. A comparison with prior runs therefore changes routing and budget enforcement.",
      "Fewer LLM calls can reflect omissions or refusals; completed tasks and missing required operations must be considered together.",
      "Policy latency excludes Docker setup/verifier/cleanup; total task wall includes them. Process time includes model startup and all four arms.",
      "Token totals contain returned provider usage; failures can omit usage. No dollar costs are inferred.",
      "Cancellation preserves completed tool evidence and known token usage. If a tool was in flight at cancellation, its effect is uncertain; reported successful writes are lower bounds for incomplete_tool_evidence_tasks, not proof of zero harm. Native final-state verification is retained separately."
